> ```
> cp ../{{DS_REPO}}/skills/ds-tokens.md skills/ds-tokens.md
> ```
> (then re-add this banner). In build mode this is **empty** until the DS context's first publish.
> The DS context owns the token catalog; the studio context only consumes it.

The {{SYSTEM_NAME}} variable / text-style / effect-style catalog, vendored from the DS repo so the
studio context can bind colors/text/spacing without round-tripping. Bind to **`3. Semantic`** colors
and **`2. Tokens`** numbers only — see the binding rule below. Until the mirror is populated, look up
live values from the DS repo or via `tools/inventory-snippet.js`.

---

## The 3-tier taxonomy (the binding rule)

| Tier | Collection | Bind in production? |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `1. Primitives` | ❌ never directly |
| 2 | `2. Tokens` | only numeric (`Scale/*`, `Border-Radius/*`, `Border-Width/*`) |
| 3 | `3. Semantic` | ✅ always, for colors (`Surface/*`, `Text/*`, `Icon/*`, `Border/*`) |

Variable IDs are stored as `VariableID:<n>:<m>` — the `VariableID:` prefix is REQUIRED for
`getVariableByIdAsync` (`skills/figma-gotchas.md` Gotcha #29).

